/*
  SettingField.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0213 · SettingField (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface (table "SettingField"). These
  entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time;
  they are kept in a per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own
  strings without editing the shared catalog.

  The web source (features/settings/components/SettingField.tsx) extracts NO strings of
  its own — the `label` and the help `i18nKey`/`content` are supplied by the parent
  call-site. The only keys this surface owns are the native accessibility chrome of its
  inline help trigger, which the web `<HelpIcon>` resolves through the global `t()`:
    • a11y.helpFor          — web `t('a11y.helpFor', { field })`  → "Help for {{field}}"
    • help.tooltip.iconLabel — web `t('help.tooltip.iconLabel')`  → generic "More info"
  Keeping these out of the Swift sources is what lets the views hold no English literals.

  The settingField.preview.* keys back the DEBUG-only Xcode previews and are not part of
  the shipped surface.
*/

/* --- Native chrome: inline help accessibility (web <HelpIcon> aria-label) --- */
"a11y.helpFor" = "Help for %@";
"help.tooltip.iconLabel" = "More info";

/* --- DEBUG previews only --- */
"settingField.preview.displayName" = "Display Name";
"settingField.preview.apiToken" = "API Token";
"settingField.preview.region" = "Region";
"settingField.preview.nickname" = "Vehicle Nickname";
"settingField.preview.help" = "This name appears on your dashboard and in shared links.";
"settingField.preview.prompt" = "Enter a value";
